# Which Python the updater wrappers should use.
#
# OPTIONAL. Delete this file (or never create it) to let `updater.sh` and
# `updater.bat` find a Python themselves. Copy it to `python.env` and edit the
# path only if your Python is not on PATH -- portable builds, embeddable
# packages, a version installed somewhere unusual, or one of several Pythons
# where the first one on PATH is not the one holding D3TA1L3R.
#
# This file is machine-local, so `python.env` is gitignored; only this example
# is tracked. Never commit a real one.
#
# Precedence, first match wins:
#   1. the 2PY2 environment variable   (overrides this file)
#   2. this file
#   3. .venv, d3ta1l3r on PATH, then any python3/python that imports d3ta1l3r
#
# 2PY2 means "a second Python" -- NOT Python 2.
#
# Formats accepted (first usable value wins; comments and blank lines ignored):

PYTHON=/usr/local/bin/python3.11

# The same value under any of these names also works:
#   PYTHON_PATH=...   PYTHON_EXE=...   PYTHON_BIN=...   PYTHON_HOME=...   2PY2=...
#
# ...or just a bare path on its own line, with no KEY= at all:
#   /usr/local/bin/python3.11
#
# Quotes are allowed and stripped, so paths with spaces are fine:
#   PYTHON="C:\Program Files\Python311\python.exe"
#
# `d3ta1l3r update` itself does not read this file: when you run it directly it
# is already running under some Python, and uses that one. These wrappers exist
# for the case where you have not settled that question yet.
